TJR wrote:
>
> Your arch-lich will resist all further attempts to polymorph it. See
> http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/monster_magic_resistance for why.

With the caveat that Ls don't eat so it's very easy for them to go
ferral.  Some folks use a pet L to kill everything in mine town then
take it down stairs and abandon it there forever.  Get good use out of
the pet then reduce risk.

> Generally, when improving pets with a polytrap, I keep balrogs, the
> better major demons, vampires, titans, mind flayers, winged gargoyles,
> and jabberwocks. A balrog is by far the best result. Sadly, you cannot
> get a tame archon this way.

Nice list and advice.  Plus keep the ones that resist magic because
polymorph no longer works on them.


